\n" [:option {:value "159388"} "Quadruple Sculls, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159400"} "Coxless Pairs, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159415"} "Coxless Fours, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159427"} "Eights, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159436"} "Lightweight Double Sculls, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159456"} "Lightweight Coxless Fours, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159471"} "Single Sculls, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "159486"} "Double Sculls, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "159498"} "Quadruple Sculls, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "159519"} "Eights, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "159527"} "Lightweight Double Sculls, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "158759"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "158882"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "159001"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "159138"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "159318"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "159686"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "159864"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "261120"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "319018"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "354091"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19008559"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2012555"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/396"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Coxless Pairs, Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "21 – 27 July 1996"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/718"} "Lake Sidney Lanier, Gainesville, Georgia"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/159507"} "26 from 13 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The defending Olympic champions, Canadians " [:a {:href "/athletes/36041"} "Marnie McBean"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/36029"} "Kathleen Heddle"] ", elected to compete in the double sculls instead (where they won gold), leaving the field for the women’s coxless pairs at the 1996 Summer Olympics somewhat more open. As reigning World Champions, Australians " [:a {:href "/athletes/35338"} "Megan Still"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/35336"} "Kate Slatter"] " were probably the favorites, although they were certain to face a strong challenge from France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/36831"} "Christine Gossé"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/36824"} "Hélène Cortin"] ", the 1993 and 1994 World Champions. In fact, Gossé had come in third at the 1995 edition only in Cortin’s absence. The United States, the reigning Pan American champion, brought its 1995 World runners-up " [:a {:href "/athletes/40508"} "Missy Schwen"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/40478"} "Karen Kraft"] " to Atlanta. The only other nation to have won a World Championship medal in the last three years, Romania, sent sisters " [:a {:href "/athletes/39487"} "Liliana"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/39486"} "Angela Cazac"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Australians got off to a strong start in the opening round by posting the fastest time, while France and the United States won the other two heats. The United States, however, mounted a serious challenge in the semi-finals and overtook the Australians to win their heat, while France coasted to an easier victory in its heat and Romania was eliminated. It might have seemed that the Australians were merely conserving their strength but, in the final, they went head to head against the Americans. Although they won gold in Olympic record time, they did so by only a 0.39 second margin of victory. The United States thus took silver and France, who had the only crew anywhere near the two front runners, captured bronze."] "\n\n" [:p {} "1996 Quadruple Sculls, Women"